ZORR MODE

LOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER
ROLE = TECH / RIGGED HUMANOID + COMBAT MOTION BASE
OWNER_DIRECTIVE = `продолжать на открытых кодах; сделать уверенную базу`
STATE = AUTHORIZED / EXECUTION REQUIRED / OWNER NOT A TECHNICAL COURIER
PARENT = #221
MAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`
SOURCE_SCENE_BRANCH = `lester/babylon-cinematic-scene-r01`
SOURCE_SCENE_HEAD = `69bec491c0aa7afb44d51d1e1b045f3c8c22c77a`
SOURCE_SCENE_COMMIT = `feat(directing): build OxiHuman blade-dodge scene R03`

## WHY R04 EXISTS
The rejected mannequin path is permanently out. #221 already records the root cause: pseudo-3D capsules/ellipses, ~4.76-head proportions, no skeleton/landmarks, no real depth, no quantitative anatomy QC.

R03 improved the scene materially and is now actually present on the Babylon branch at `69bec491...`: pinned OxiHuman GLB, real Babylon glTF loader, two real meshes, blade-dodge geometry, existing scene/set/camera intent. Preserve that evidence. Do not regress to primitives or 2D construction.

R04 strengthens the base from a one-shot deformed mesh into a reusable ADULT RIGGED HUMANOID + OPEN MOCAP pipeline.

## REQUIRED OSS STACK — PINNED
### Adult human generator / rig
Use MakeHuman/MPFB2 as the primary adult-body and rigging authority for this base.

- repo: https://github.com/makehumancommunity/mpfb2
- release: `v2.0.17`
- exact tag commit: `80919fa4682335c41847f761a4d79dcad4124732`
- source code license: GPLv3
- bundled/core graphical assets (base mesh, proxies, targets, clothes, rigs, poses, etc.): CC0 1.0
- official license: https://github.com/makehumancommunity/mpfb2/blob/v2.0.17/LICENSE.md
- no third-party community asset may enter unless its exact per-asset license is separately proven.

Prefer MPFB standard or Rigify workflow. The result must be a real skinned mesh driven by an armature; no image-space anatomy and no smooth whole-surface vertex warp as the primary action mechanism.

### Motion retargeter
Use a mature OSS Blender retargeter rather than writing a ZORR retargeter.

Primary candidate:
- repo: https://github.com/Mwni/blender-animation-retargeting
- exact commit: `424f08bd7e675619adf539209a1e8816c242c386`
- version at that commit: `2.4.0`
- license: GPL-3.0-or-later
- Blender minimum: 4.4

Use Blender 4.5 LTS or another compatible open Blender build unless exact environment evidence proves a better pinned version.

If this retargeter fails on the chosen MPFB rig after one evidence-backed attempt, do not tread water. Inspect a mature OSS fallback (MakeWalk / Diffeomorphic or another proven Blender retargeter) and record the reason for switching. No Auto-Rig Pro, Mixamo dependency, proprietary animation service, paid plugin, or remote inference.

### Open combat / interaction motion source
Primary motion dataset: Carnegie Mellon University Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database.

- official database: https://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/
- database states motions are free for all uses.
- attacker candidates: Subject #2, trials #7/#8/#9 = `swordplay`, 120 fps; trial #5 = `punch/strike`.
- paired-interaction timing/spacing candidate: Subjects #22 and #23, trial #20 = `violence - A picks up high stool, threatens to strike B`, two synchronized subjects, 120 fps.

Do NOT blindly accept a clip because the label sounds right. Visually inspect the motion. The final selected defender must show an actual evasive response / readable avoidance. If #23/20 does not, reject it and search the same open CMU database or another mature open mocap source before hand-authoring action.

Do not commit raw third-party source data unless redistribution terms are explicitly proven. Record source URL/subject/trial/hash and keep only the legally safe derived baked result when appropriate.

## REUSE ORDER
1. Existing #221 Babylon branch/head and R03 set/camera/action measurements.
2. MPFB2 core CC0 adult mesh + rig.
3. Mature OSS retargeter.
4. Open mocap clip(s).
5. Native Blender bake/export -> glTF/GLB.
6. Existing Babylon `@babylonjs/loaders` path.
7. Minimal glue only where unavoidable.

Do NOT create a new anatomy system, custom retargeting algorithm, procedural humanoid body, or 2D fallback.

## BASE A — WHITE-STAGE ANATOMY PASS
Before the cinematic set, prove the character base on a plain white/neutral stage.

Required frame:
- exactly two adult humanoid meshes generated from the same proven MPFB/MakeHuman basis;
- real skinned geometry + armatures;
- full bodies entirely visible, including hairless head silhouette, hands and footwear/bare feet as applicable;
- both actors on the same physical ground plane;
- no foot sinking, floating, body intersection, camera clipping, or cropped sword;
- neutral white/near-white background and floor; no decorative environment masking silhouette errors;
- real 3D lights/depth/occlusion.

Quantitative anatomy gate:
- reject child/chibi proportions;
- measured standing head-to-body ratio must be adult-range; target ~7.5 heads, acceptable 7.0–8.3 unless a documented character-specific reason overrides it;
- record height, head height, shoulder width, hip height and foot-to-ground error for each actor;
- max static foot-to-ground error <= 0.01 m in the white-stage proof.

Output evidence must include a 1280x720 PNG plus machine-readable measurement/provenance JSON.

## BASE B — RIG + MOTION PASS
Prove that the action is skeletal animation, not surface warping.

Required:
- source armature and target MPFB armature documented;
- explicit bone mapping artifact/preset where the chosen retargeter supports one;
- baked target animation on the MPFB rig;
- no per-frame ZORR vertex deformation used as the primary motion source;
- inspect feet/hands and apply the retargeter's native correction facilities where necessary;
- record selected source clip identifiers and frame/time window.

## BASE C — ATTACK / DODGE PASS
Required final action frame/short clip:
- attacker owns a real 3D sword (blade + grip + crossguard);
- grip/weapon transform is parented/constrained to the attacker's hand/wrist bone, not visually placed nearby;
- defender visibly evades the strike;
- no blade/body penetration at the selected proof frame;
- minimum measured blade-to-defender mesh clearance must be > 0.03 m and < 0.20 m so it reads as a near miss, with ~0.08–0.12 m preferred;
- at least one physically plausible support foot per actor remains grounded through the selected action beat; report worst ground-contact error;
- both full silhouettes and the entire blade remain inside frame;
- action direction is immediately readable without captions.

Reuse the R03 spatial/camera intent as the first target:
- attacker around `[-0.62, 0, 0.05] m`, yaw `-8 deg`;
- dodger around `[0.62, 0, -0.05] m`, yaw `+15 deg`;
- blade length `1.08 m`;
- R03 reference near-miss clearance `0.0970096418 m`;
- camera position `[3.10, 1.55, 3.65] m`;
- target `[0.12, 1.02, -0.38] m`;
- vertical FOV `39 deg`.

These are starting measurements, not permission to fake the new rigged action. Adjust only when measured rig/mocap geometry requires it, and record the delta.

## BASE D — BABYLON PASS
Bring the baked rigged GLB into the EXISTING Babylon scene path.

Required:
- use existing `@babylonjs/core` / `@babylonjs/loaders` versions already pinned by #221 unless a proven blocker requires a controlled change;
- real Babylon camera/lights/depth;
- white-stage proof remains reproducible separately;
- cinematic brutalist set remains reusable separately from actors;
- exported scene/manifest records mesh, rig, animation, mocap, tool and license provenance;
- deterministic 1280x720 capture in the pinned environment;
- fresh tests + strict typecheck + production build + Chromium capture evidence on exact HEAD;
- no claim of PASS unless exact-head evidence is green.

## EXPECTED ARTIFACTS
Names may vary only if consistently documented, but deliver equivalents of:
- white-stage two-adult anatomy PNG;
- attack/dodge PNG;
- rigged animated GLB used by Babylon;
- motion/bone-mapping or retarget preset artifact;
- measurement QC JSON;
- OSS provenance manifest;
- exact-head CI/run evidence and hashes.

## FAIL-CLOSED RULES
- chibi/low-poly/gamey body as primary physiology base = FAIL;
- capsule/ellipse/procedural mannequin body = FAIL;
- hand-painted or PIL 2D character = FAIL;
- primary action made by whole-mesh vertex warp = FAIL for R04;
- floating blade = FAIL;
- penetrated defender = FAIL;
- cropped feet/blade = FAIL;
- unverified third-party asset license = FAIL;
- proprietary/paid/closed retarget or mocap path = FAIL;
- visual sanity without measured anatomy/ground/blade QC = NOT PASS;
- implementer-only claim without independent DUNCAN verification = NOT FINAL PASS.

MERGE = NO
CANON = NO
PRODUCTION_CHARACTER_TRUTH_WRITEBACK = NO
OWNER_REVIEW_REQUIRED_FOR_FINAL_VISUAL_ACCEPTANCE = YES
NEXT = LESTER builds BASE A -> B -> C -> D on OSS-only stack, persists exact evidence; DUNCAN independently verifies exact delivered HEAD. Owner must not act as technical courier.
